    "type": "Site page",
    "text": "LEARNING & RESEARCH Opportunities Interested in adaptive optics, optical engineering or astronomical instruments? Explore ways students and early-career researchers may connect with our work at INAF Padova. About availability. This page describes possible pathways and areas of interest. It is not a list of confirmed open positions, thesis assignments or funded internships. Any arrangement depends on a suitable supervisor, resources and the applicable institutional procedures. Master’s theses ↓ PhD research ↓ Internships ↓ Other opportunities ↓ 01 / STUDY Master’s thesis projects Master’s students in astronomy, physics, optics, engineering, computing and related disciplines may explore a research thesis connected to our instruments or laboratory activities. Possible projects range from numerical modelling to experimental optical work or astronomical data analysis. Potential directions Wavefront sensing and adaptive-optics simulations Laboratory calibration, alignment and optical metrology Instrument performance analysis and data reduction Optical design, system modelling and verification These are illustrative research directions, not pre-approved thesis titles. The topic, academic supervisor and assessment requirements must be agreed with the student's university. Explore research themes ↗ Find a potential supervisor ↗ 02 / RESEARCH PhD research Doctoral research can investigate adaptive-optics concepts, laser and natural guide-star sensing, image reconstruction, astronomical instrumentation and the science enabled by these technologies. Topics may be developed with university and instrument-project collaborators. Possible research themes Multi-conjugate adaptive optics, wavefront sensing and control Calibration, point-spread-function modelling and diagnostics Instrument development, verification and commissioning High-angular-resolution astronomical observations PhD admission and funded positions are governed by the official university calls ; discussing a research idea with ADOPT does not constitute an offer of admission or funding. University of Padova PhD calls ↗ PhD programme directory ↗ 03 / EXPERIENCE Internships & placements Depending on the needs and capacity of current projects, a training placement might involve optical-bench experiments, software development, numerical simulations, systems engineering or astronomical data handling. What to consider Internships may be curricular or linked to a formal university training programme. A placement requires suitable supervision and any necessary agreement, insurance and authorisation between the institutions. Duration, eligibility, location and funding—if any—must be confirmed before arrangements are made. Students from the University of Padova should consult its internship office and the requirements of their individual degree programme. Students from other universities should first confirm their home institution's procedures. University of Padova internships ↗ Contact information ↗ 04 / COLLABORATE Research visits & formal positions Short research visits, scientific collaborations and other training activities may be possible by prior agreement. Research appointments, fellowships and technical posts, when available, follow the relevant INAF or partner-institution selection procedures. For officially advertised openings, consult the formal INAF or partner-institution call rather than treating an informal enquiry as an application. The Media INAF roundup is informational and may be incomplete or out of date. Media INAF calls roundup (unofficial) ↗ Our team ↗ Research areas to explore Examples of ongoing group research, not a catalogue of available placements. WAVEFRONT SENSING INGOT Laser-guide-star sensors and laboratory testing ↗ ADAPTIVE OPTICS MATTO Multi-conjugate adaptive-optics experiments ↗ CALIBRATION MAVIS Optical systems and adaptive-optics calibration ↗ INSTRUMENT ENGINEERING SOXS Instrument integration, verification and spectroscopy ↗ GET IN TOUCH How to enquire Find a relevant group member using the People directory , then contact them through an appropriate institutional channel. Briefly describe your interests and mention the type of opportunity you are seeking. Your degree programme, university and current stage of study The research area or project that interests you Your approximate start date and available duration A short CV and any academic or internship requirements Informal enquiries do not replace official applications. Please do not send sensitive personal documents until requested through an authorised process. Meet the group ↗ General guidance reviewed 31 October 2026. For rules, eligibility, vacancies and deadlines, follow the official linked institutions."
