    "text": "← All group members Optical alignment Remon VanGaalen Doctoral researcher · INAF Padova collaboration Studies calibration and non-common-path aberration characterisation for NIRVANA-VIS, with wider adaptive-optics testing interests. About Remon undertakes doctoral research linked to advanced adaptive-optics instrumentation at INAF Padova. A public AO4ELT conference programme identifies his work on non-common-path aberration characterisation for NIRVANA-VIS. That topic connects calibration, optical modelling and test procedures to reliable performance of a complex telescope instrument. Projects NIRVANA-VIS A visible-light upgrade of LINC-NIRVANA, combining adaptive optics and speckle holography. MAVIS Adaptive-optics-assisted visible-light imaging and spatially resolved spectroscopy. iD ORCiD 0000-0003-1556-0345 ↗ Research & profile links AO4ELT research programme ↗ Doctoral research topic ↗ 2026 research presentation ↗ ADOPT Adaptive optics and astronomical instrumentation at INAF Padova. Group contact information → Suggest an update to this profile →"
